WEBVTT

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:13.180
Romeo's Blue Skies

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.820
"To the Sky..."

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.880
<i>Overlooking the rows of houses and stores</i>

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.290
<i>from the highest vantage,</i>

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:27.400
<i>Such things as tears and sadness</i>

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.540
<i>will quickly vanish</i>

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.100
<i>The birds, wind, and sunshine...</i>

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:41.290
<i>...all are your friends</i>

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:46.360
<i>I'll carry this dream farther than far</i>

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.450
<i>...no matter the distance...</i>

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:58.210
<i>I long to fly freely</i>

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.490
<i>through the blue sky in my heart...</i>

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:05.420
<i>The far distant blue sky</i>

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:12.870
<i>It flows into tomorrow</i>

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:25.180
Takara Fansubs

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:30.770
<i>Romeo had believed Anzelmo was his friend.</i>

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:35.220
<i>But Anzelmo had lured him into a trap.</i>

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:41.240
<i>Unjustly accused of theft, Romeo was forced to run away.</i>

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:48.620
<i>But the Wolf Pack had been duped by Anzelmo, and they were lying in ambush for him.</i>

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:57.080
Episode 13:

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:57.080
Reunion in the Sewer

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.630
You stinking coward!

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:19.200
"Coward"...??

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:23.360
You sold us out to the cops!
- You're gonna pay!

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:24.510
W..Wait!

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:27.840
What are you talking about?
I didn't do anything like that!

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:30.150
Why you bastard..!
Still playing dumb, are you?

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:36.480
What's going on in here?

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:42.230
You fellows have been pilfering goods from here for quite some time now, I hear.

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:43.770
Oh shit... run!

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:49.040
Who called for help?
Which one of you is Romeo?

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:55.720
You let the cops in on the whole thing beforehand!

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.340
You led us into a trap!

00:02:58.540 --> 00:02:59.600
Trap?

00:02:59.710 --> 00:03:02.370
I don't have the faintest idea what you're talking about! <i>- Shut up!</i>

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:07.660
Get him!

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:10.090
Wait, for God's sakes! I don't..!
- Shaddap!

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:15.070
It's too early for you to go nighty-night just yet!

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.090
You're a bad guy!

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.490
Ouch! I can't breathe!

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:29.130
He cut loose!

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:30.790
Chase after him!

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.950
Hurry up! Get after him!

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:47.080
Thanks, you saved my life back there!

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:51.570
What's going on, anyways? I didn't sell out the Wolf Pack to the police!

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:56.640
Shit! Where'd he get off to?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:09.210
Found him?
- No, not yet.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.250
Find that bastard NOW!
So we can punch his face in!

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.000
Hey!

00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:37.880
He ran up this street!

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.790
Any trace of him?
- No shadow, no nothing!

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.320
Find him! He's gotta be around here somewhere!

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:53.380
There he is!

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:01.310
Oh no!

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:09.310
I'll fix you so you won't be able to pull any more tricks!

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.420
Just try! I won't be beat that easily!

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.810
Is that the best you can do?

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:20.970
Now! Apologize!

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:21.900
No!

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:23.090
What a pigheaded ass you are!

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.260
Stop that!

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:27.700
Cease at once!

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:29.080
Who are you?!

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:33.450
Stay away from that fellow...!
For your own sakes!

00:05:33.580 --> 00:05:34.770
What's your game?

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:39.660
...for there is a dark curse hanging upon this dreadful boy's shoulders!

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:49.540
Whosoever strikes him shall fall dead on the spot, rest assured!

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.590
Hmph! Right!

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:55.450
To believe or not to believe... is up to you.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.690
Shut up, you!
Scram before you get hurt.

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:00.740
Ah, pathetic fellow!
- Say what?!

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:05.230
No one can save you from the curse this boy carries! Not even I!

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:06.420
Hmph! How absurd.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:10.740
Ohh...! The pain! Help me...!

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:14.180
And look! The police!
- Police?

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:21.830
There's no police there!

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:27.080
He disappeared!

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:30.250
What's going on here?

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:44.090
What a dope! That was a cinch!
- Uh... Umm...

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:46.890
Long time no see, Romeo!

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:52.640
D... Dante!

00:06:57.210 --> 00:07:01.790
<i>Romeo remembered the night of the great storm on the lake,</i>

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:06.350
<i>...the night he was torn from Dante and his companions.</i>

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:14.440
Dante! So you're still alive!
- Same to you!

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:17.550
I thought you gave up the ghost a long time ago!

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.600
It'll take more than that to do me in!

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:21.740
Hah! Big talker!

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:24.710
You low-life!

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:27.800
Same to you! You've got the devil's luck on your side!

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:30.840
What!? Now you've said it! Let's tumble!
- Let's go!

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:36.000
Why you..!

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:42.020
Romeo!

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:46.010
D... Don't spook me like that!

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:51.210
Sorry. I sneaked into the big masked ball earlier.

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.150
This stuff came in pretty handy.

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:56.680
You really rescued me.
Thank you, Dante.

00:07:57.050 --> 00:08:00.470
Oh, don't mention it. Nothing's too big for Dante the Great!

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:07.280
Afterwards I ended up here in Milan, working as a chimney sweep...

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:08.360
So...

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.570
So, you're a chimney sweep, too.

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:14.090
"Romeo," was it?

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.920
The kid stole a hefty sum, from what they say.

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:21.450
Sounds like one wicked little monster, all right.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:25.060
He's probably still nearby.
Let's split up and search for him.

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:25.950
Understood.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:43.980
Are you...?
- ...being chased, yeah.

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.840
If they catch me, they'll send me to prison.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:47.860
To prison?!

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:02.070
Romeo.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:07.160
Anzelmo.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:10.160
Anzelmo!

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.320
Where's Romeo?

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:27.930
<i>Angeletta was the only one who knew the truth.</i>

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:31.960
<i>...that Romeo was accused of Anzelmo's crimes.</i>

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:49.700
Please, Anzelmo, tell Mother and Father the truth!

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:54.400
Hmph! I don't get it. Why do you stick up for him like that?

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:56.030
He's my friend.

00:09:56.520 --> 00:09:57.640
Your friend?!

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.140
...my first friend.

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:03.220
No... he's not the first...

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:06.150
My first friend was...

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:07.650
...Anzelmo!

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:14.680
When I was little, you used to come and play with me, here in my room.

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:19.350
Big Brother!

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:25.320
You were so gentle with me...
You were so gentle, back then.

00:10:30.390 --> 00:10:31.610
Please, big brother!

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:33.700
Tell them the truth...
- Stop that!

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:36.680
You're not even my real sister!

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:40.970
You were gonna tell them anyways, weren't you?

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:45.890
So tell them! But Mom and Dad won't believe anyone but me!

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:49.720
After all, I'm their real son.
Not some homeless girl.

00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:27.720
Okay, nobody'll find us here.

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:29.620
This spot should hold up for a while as a hideout.

00:11:31.070 --> 00:11:34.690
What a kick, though!
You don't seem like the thieving kind.

00:11:46.790 --> 00:11:50.320
I won't tell anyone!
It'll be our secret, the three of us.

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:54.240
Forget about me..!
So long as you're okay...

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:06.470
I was taken for a ride!

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:08.350
You coward!

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:12.050
You sold the Wolf Pack to the cops!

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:16.770
I see it, now... I finally get it. It was all part of Anzelmo's schemes.

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:21.240
Sounds likely. You're way too friendly with folks.

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:23.160
I didn't steal a thing!

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:28.850
What could I possibly do to get the boss to believe me?

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:30.700
You shouldn't do anything, and you know it.

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:34.270
That's the way adults are, it's that simple.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:35.940
But if I don't...

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:37.200
Enough on that.

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:41.260
Listen, tomorrow there's a ride going to Venice.
- To Venice?

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:43.750
If you were alone, you could sneak on.

00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:44.360
Eh??

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:47.320
You can bail out of this hole!

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:50.530
Figure out your next move once you get to Venice.

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:51.370
Yes, but...

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:58.730
I don't want to run away... Not while I've been pegged a thief.

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:01.250
Can you afford to be talking like that?

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:03.650
If they catch you, you're headed up the river, you know!

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:14.410
Whoa! Better be heading back. So long!

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:15.880
Um, Dante!

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:19.080
Got it? You're busting out of Milan tomorrow!

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:25.290
<i>Dante was right.</i>

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:29.440
<i>Romeo's only option left was to flee Milan.</i>

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:35.900
<i>But that meant never seeing Angeletta again.</i>

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:40.940
Umm... mm... and this word is... is...

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.660
"Bird"!
- Oh right! Bird!

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.500
I'm hopeless at this.
I forget so quickly!

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:49.830
No, no, you're remembering, bit by bit.

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:55.760
I'll bet by springtime you'll be able to read the whole book.

00:13:55.950 --> 00:13:58.140
All right, I'll try to live up to that!

00:13:58.820 --> 00:14:02.260
And by that time, you've got to be feeling well again, hear?

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:09.270
Angeletta...

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:14.400
Angeletta couldn't believe it...

00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:17.090
...when she heard you were a thief.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:19.250
She said how betrayed she felt.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:26.000
<i>I can't bear to say goodbye as things stand now!</i>

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:29.920
<i>Please believe in me, Angeletta!</i>

00:14:52.230 --> 00:14:53.150
Nikita!

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:56.300
Hey, it was really something last night! Wow!

00:14:56.520 --> 00:14:59.810
We cornered that guy Romeo in the alleyway.

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:04.660
Say Nikita, why didn't you come with us?

00:15:06.310 --> 00:15:08.760
Don't you want to hit Romeo, Nikita?

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:13.500
Why would I? What's the point in hitting a guy like that?

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:25.070
What's wrong?
- Those guys...!

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:29.700
The "merchandise"...?

00:15:30.050 --> 00:15:31.110
All packed up!

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:35.320
I'll bet they're planning something again.

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:46.340
Oh! It's Romeo!

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:53.750
What's he up to?

00:15:57.030 --> 00:15:58.640
You're gonna slip into one of those boxes.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:01.480
So I stow away on there and I'll be on my way to Venice?

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:02.300
Right!

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:03.750
Freedom's a-waiting!

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:23.060
Haven't they found Romeo yet?

00:16:23.790 --> 00:16:26.920
Unbelievable! What can those idiots possibly be doing?

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:32.080
You know, some coins have been disappearing here and there lately.

00:16:32.210 --> 00:16:34.500
That kid just may be responsible.

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:37.390
Anzelmo.

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:41.380
How are you feeling, does it still hurt?

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:43.340
No, I'm okay now.

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:44.570
That's good.

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:48.450
Romeo! Everything comes back to him! It's all his fault.

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:52.000
It was our mistake for having bought him in the first place.

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:24.950
Angeletta.

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:28.080
What's wrong? Not feeling good?

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:34.140
Angeletta!

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:36.280
Wh... What is it, for God's sake?!

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:40.160
Come, tell me all about it.

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:44.790
Tell me, Angeletta.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:48.930
Bring Romeo back here!

00:17:49.570 --> 00:17:51.340
I saw it...
- Saw it...?

00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:56.230
It... wasn't Romeo who was stealing.

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:00.400
It wasn't him?

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:04.230
Well, now, then... what?

00:18:04.610 --> 00:18:07.560
Did the money just get up and walk off all by itself?

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:13.620
Edda! Give her a chance to speak.

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:19.150
Hmph! So, you're saying you saw who stole it?

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:21.450
Who was it, then, if it wasn't Romeo?

00:18:22.590 --> 00:18:23.470
Was it you?

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:26.560
It certainly wasn't me.

00:18:27.420 --> 00:18:28.570
And, of course, not Anzel...

00:18:34.890 --> 00:18:37.580
Was it Anzelmo? It was, wasn't it!

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:42.190
Yes.

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:51.600
Please, don't scold Anzelmo too much.

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:52.660
Why?

00:18:53.760 --> 00:18:58.480
I can't stand seeing anybody at home looking sad.

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:00.240
Angeletta!

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:04.760
Ohh, what a generous child!

00:19:05.460 --> 00:19:10.670
As you wish. Anything you want!
We'll give you all you ask for!

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:13.090
We'll bring back Romeo!

00:19:14.880 --> 00:19:15.600
Really?

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:19.480
Of course really! You needn't worry about a thing.

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:23.540
Thank you, Mother!

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:28.340
It's bad for you to have so many things running around in your head.

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:30.180
Now, good night!

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:31.270
Yes ma'am.

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:40.000
You said you'd bring Romeo back...

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:42.230
...but what about the police...?
- Dear!!

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:46.750
Do you want my Anzelmo to be called a thief by everyone?

00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:52.170
We never had that conversation.
Not me! And not you!

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:53.780
Got it?

00:19:58.230 --> 00:20:01.250
Mom! I'm hungry!
- Oh, oh, yes, of course!

00:20:01.380 --> 00:20:04.050
I'll prepare some snacks for you right away.

00:20:16.750 --> 00:20:19.960
Thank goodness, Romeo!
Thank goodness!

00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:25.960
Dante, on second thought, I really want to tell Angeletta...

00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:27.590
You idiot, now's not the time for that!

00:20:29.840 --> 00:20:31.210
Do it right!

00:20:43.150 --> 00:20:44.610
Take care, Romeo!

00:20:44.920 --> 00:20:48.860
Is this carriage headed to Venice?
- Yes, we'll be off soon.

00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:50.650
To Venice?!

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:55.760
Crap! I mixed them up!

00:20:57.790 --> 00:20:59.220
Then, where is that carriage...??

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:03.340
Why... you... OAF!
- Say what?!

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:06.410
Wh... What's with this guy?!

00:21:06.490 --> 00:21:09.400
Do you know where that carriage is headed? Do you?!

00:21:09.470 --> 00:21:10.920
How should I?

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:14.720
Those two are armed robbers!
The luggage is full of gunpowder!

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:17.450
Say what?! Romeo..!

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:25.580
Don't shake it so much. Do you want the powder to go up?

00:21:26.530 --> 00:21:30.340
Makes you sweat, don't it? One slip and we're pushing daisies!

00:21:56.220 --> 00:21:59.020
I had snuck onto a robber's buggy!

00:21:59.680 --> 00:22:01.090
The compartment was full of gunpowder!

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:05.260
They planned to blow up a police station to free a friend!

00:22:05.810 --> 00:22:07.590
Somebody, help!

00:22:08.340 --> 00:22:11.500
See you then!

00:22:08.340 --> 00:22:11.500
<i>Escape, Quickly!</i>

00:22:08.340 --> 00:22:11.500
Next time:

00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:17.480
<i>"Si Si Ciao ~ On These Roman Roofs"</i>

00:22:26.090 --> 00:22:30.190
<i>Si Si Ciao, why do the good times</i>

00:22:30.290 --> 00:22:34.490
<i>seem to end so soon?</i>

00:22:34.690 --> 00:22:38.690
<i>Si Si Ciao, we're all friends</i>

00:22:38.890 --> 00:22:42.890
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>

00:22:43.500 --> 00:22:47.800
<i>Your laughing voice dances</i>

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:51.700
<i>Once again in the sky</i>

00:22:52.100 --> 00:22:59.000
<i>Your pocket bursting with memories</i>

00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:04.600
<i>Si Si Ciao, goodbye but for now</i>

00:23:04.800 --> 00:23:08.800
<i>Let's meet again on these Roman roofs</i>
